cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Compact-Image Obstructions for a Hyperbolic Grading in Sp(32,32): Neutral, Grading-Even, and Extremal Order Parameters"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Hernandez
    given-names: Joseph
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    email: joe@disruptionjoe.com
date-released: 2026-08-03
version: 1.0.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/disruptionjoe/gu-formalization"
abstract: >-
  Three finite-dimensional compact-image obstructions are proved for
  stabilizers of continuously neutral vectors, grading-even operators, and
  sign-matched extremal-weight vectors. The hypotheses are verified directly
  for a hyperbolic grading in Sp(32,32), whose positive and negative adjoint
  eigenspaces are 2080-dimensional abelian spaces of square-zero quaternionic
  matrices. The paper separates continuous neutrality, discrete operator
  parity, and extremal weight and states precise algebraic and physical scope
  boundaries.
keywords:
  - compact-image obstruction
  - Sp(32,32)
  - quaternionic symplectic group
  - hyperbolic grading
  - parabolic grading
  - extremal weight
  - invariant inner product
  - stabilizer
